{
  "id": "27987_furiyamu",
  "headword": "{降|ふ}り{止|や}む",
  "reading": "ふりやむ",
  "romaji": "furiyamu",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (godan)",
  "gloss": "to stop raining; to stop falling (of rain or snow)",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to stop raining; to stop (of rain or snow)",
      "explanation": "Of rain, snow, or hail, to cease falling. A compound of {降|ふ}る (to fall as precipitation) + {止|や}む (to stop)."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "27987_furiyamu_ex1",
      "japanese": "{雨|あめ}がやっと{降|ふ}り{止|や}んだ。",
      "english": "The rain has finally stopped.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "27987_furiyamu_ex2",
      "japanese": "{雪|ゆき}が{降|ふ}り{止|や}むのを{待|ま}った。",
      "english": "I waited for the snow to stop falling.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "27987_furiyamu_ex3",
      "japanese": "{夜中|よなか}に{雨|あめ}が{降|ふ}り{止|や}んで、{朝|あさ}には{青空|あおぞら}が{広|ひろ}がっていた。",
      "english": "The rain stopped during the night, and by morning a blue sky had spread out.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Intransitive ({自動詞|じどうし}). A compound of {降|ふ}る + {止|や}む, used only for precipitation (rain, snow, hail).\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {雨|あめ}・{雪|ゆき}が{降|ふ}り{止|や}む: the rain or snow stops\n\nASPECT (ている):\n- {降|ふ}り{止|や}んでいる = has stopped (and is still not falling) — a resulting state.\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {止|や}む: to stop (of rain, wind, sound) — {降|ふ}り{止|や}む specifies that something was falling\n- {晴|は}れる: to clear up — focuses on the sky becoming clear, not just the rain ceasing",
